{
 "id": "AT-M3-14c-c8-rare",
 "needs": [
  "types"
 ],
 "note": "AT-M3-14 (F), C8: smoke fails C8 only when the count of a rare string (a baseline count of at most c8.rare_max) or of the arm list (c8.arm_list) changes; a common word's changed count is an `info c8` line and smoke stays green. fake-claude.pl writes a stand-in binary (2.1.999: smoke takes a version-named binary's name; it exits 0 for validate and test) holding every baseline string as often as the baseline counts it, then shifts a common word, drops a rare string, or leaves an arm out of the arm list; no string is named here, each is picked from the staged baseline. The case runs on its own staged copy (stage_overlay with the baseline as staged) so steps (e) to (g) can edit the baseline (baseline-edit.pl): with 0 only the arm list fails, a string whose count equals it is rare, and without the key every string is rare, as with a malformed one (j: -1, k: not a number); (i) a baseline that does not count its arm list fails. A pass line names the rare and common counts baseline-edit.pl count reads from the staged baseline",
 "now": "2026-10-21T14:05:12+03:00",
 "tz": "Etc/GMT-3",
 "env": {
  "CLAUDE_CODE_TMPDIR": "$TMP/cct"
 },
 "stage_overlay": {
  "assets/canary-baseline.json": "$PLUGIN/assets/canary-baseline.json"
 },
 "steps": [
  {
   "name": "(a) every count as recorded: C8 passes with no info line, smokeDue cleared",
   "setup": [
    {
     "write": "$WATCH/version.json",
     "json": {
      "lastVersion": "2.1.999",
      "smokeDue": "2.1.999"
     }
    }
   ],
   "exec": [
    "/usr/bin/perl",
    "$CASE/fake-claude.pl",
    "$PLUGIN/assets/canary-baseline.json",
    "$TMP/v/2.1.999"
   ],
   "expect": {
    "exit": 0
   }
  },
  {
   "exec": [
    "/usr/bin/perl",
    "$CASE/baseline-edit.pl",
    "$PLUGIN/assets/canary-baseline.json",
    "count"
   ],
   "expect": {
    "exit": 0,
    "stdout_has": [
     "^rare \\d+ common \\d+$"
    ]
   },
   "capture": {
    "C8_RARE": "re:^rare (\\d+) common \\d+$",
    "C8_COMMON": "re:^rare \\d+ common (\\d+)$"
   }
  },
  {
   "argv": [
    "smoke",
    "--sid",
    "$SID",
    "--claude",
    "$TMP/v/2.1.999",
    "--types",
    "$TYPES"
   ],
   "expect": {
    "exit": 0,
    "stdout_has": [
     "^ok validate \\(exit 0\\)$",
     "^ok test \\(exit 0\\)$",
     "^ok c8 \\($C8_RARE rare strings and the arm list as recorded; $C8_COMMON common words not compared\\)$",
     "^ok c9 \\(6 declarations",
     "^SMOKE PASS 2\\.1\\.999\\n\\z"
    ],
    "stdout_lacks": [
     "^info c8",
     "^FAIL"
    ],
    "files": [
     {
      "path": "$WATCH/version.json",
      "keys_absent": [
       "smokeDue"
      ],
      "json": {
       "lastSmokePass": "2.1.999"
      }
     }
    ],
    "rows": [
     {
      "file": "$WATCH/$SID.classic.jsonl",
      "ev": "smoke_pass",
      "count": 1
     }
    ]
   }
  },
